// the user's prime.stex, verbatim
wts there does not exist greatest prime

afsoc there is a largest prime number. let P denote the largest prime number such that
A = {p_1, p_2, ..., P}
is the set of all prime numbers. then construct a number N such that
N = (p_1 cross p_2 cross ... cross P) + 1
note that for all p in A, N == 1 mod p implies it will always leave a remainder of 1.

qed
